---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
const lastUpdated = "August 2026";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="Important details about the technical limitations, liability protections, and accuracy standards of Pixelquil tools."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-20">
    <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full bg-brand-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-brand-600">
      Disclaimer
    </span>
    <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 sm:text-5xl">Disclaimer and Terms of Utility</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-10 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">General Information</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          All web tools, code generators, validation checkers, and technical guides published on Pixelquil are provided for general educational and informational purposes only. While every effort is made to maintain the integrity of our browser based utilities, users must independently inspect and verify all code output before deploying files to commercial, production, or high security environments.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Accuracy of Tool Outputs</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Automated conversions, code minifications, and SVG processing algorithms can occasionally generate unexpected formatting errors due to browser rendering variations or unusual input syntax. Pixelquil makes no formal warranties regarding the completeness, reliability, or absolute technical precision of processed files, calculated values, or generated configuration code.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You accept full responsibility for auditing all generated assets to ensure they conform to your project security requirements, browser support targets, and quality criteria.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Limitation of Professional Advice</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The contents of this platform do not constitute formal legal, cybersecurity, or software engineering advice. Technical explanations regarding vector security, WCAG color contrast standards, or SEO site configs are meant to serve as practical references rather than legal compliance guarantees.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          For critical infrastructure, strict regulatory requirements, or complex enterprise web systems, you should consult with a certified security auditor or software professional.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Client Side Processing and Data Handling</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Our online tools execute directly in your web browser using client side scripting technologies. Pixelquil does not upload, inspect, or store your private graphics, vector markup, or website configuration files on external servers. However, users are advised not to paste sensitive system credentials or proprietary API keys into any online validation tool on the web.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Third Party Trademarks and References</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          References to third party standards, web specifications, software frameworks, or organizations such as the World Wide Web Consortium or Google do not imply endorsement, affiliation, or sponsorship. All trademarks and brand names mentioned on this website belong to their respective owners. Official documentation from specification bodies should always be regarded as the primary authority.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Service Availability and Changes</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Pixelquil offers these web utilities on an as available basis without guaranteeing uninterrupted access or operational uptime. We reserve the right to update, modify, rebuild, or retire any tool or documentation page at any time without prior notice.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Reporting Errors</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If you encounter a bug, incorrect calculation, or outdated technical specification, please notify us through our <a href="/contact/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline font-medium">contact page</a> so we can review and resolve the issue.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</MainLayout>